    <!-- Accessibility explanation -->
    <string name="lock_explain_title">Double-tap to lock</string>
    <string name="lock_explain_body">Android only lets apps lock the screen through an Accessibility service, so this feature needs one.\n\nWhat the service does:\n• Locks the screen when you double-tap empty space on the home screen.\n• If system expansion fails, opens the notification shade on swipe down.\n\nWhat it does NOT do:\n• It cannot read the screen, what you type, or any app content.\n• This app has no internet permission, so nothing can leave your phone.\n\nNext, Android\'s Accessibility settings open. Tap \"Installed apps\" (or \"Downloaded apps\"), choose \"Minimal Launcher lock\", and turn it on.\n\nIf Android says the setting is restricted: open App info for Minimal Launcher → ⋮ menu → \"Allow restricted settings\", then try again.</string>
    <string name="lock_explain_go">Open settings</string>
    <string name="lock_service_label">Minimal Launcher lock</string>
    <string name="lock_service_desc">Lets Minimal Launcher lock the screen when you double-tap empty space on the home screen. It does not read screen content or anything you type.</string>
